#
# LeakSanitizer suppressions for tools/sanitizers/run.sh.

# Mesa's Vulkan driver (llvmpipe), started by FFmpeg's hardware probe when Qt Multimedia loads
# (Quick Look's media viewer: QFFmpeg::loadHWContext, av_hwdevice_ctx_create, libavutil's
# vulkan_device_create_internal): 128 bytes allocated once inside the driver (under pthread_once),
# reported at exit after the driver was unloaded again (its frames are "<unknown module>"). Seen on
# GitHub's ubuntu-24.04 runner (sanitizers run 38816106967, 2026-10-15), not in the same Fedora 44
# container on minihost with the same packages (mesa-vulkan-drivers 26.2.4, libavutil-free 8.1.3,
# Qt 6.11.2), where FFmpeg creates the same llvmpipe device. Nothing of Plasma Fusion calls FFmpeg
# or Vulkan; only leaks allocated below libavutil's Vulkan device creation are suppressed.
leak:vulkan_device_create_internal
